@@ -6,3 +6,15 @@ package holds the order book, in TypeScript; the shop's website and its staff to
 `src/index.ts`.
 
 Prices are integer cents everywhere. Run the tests with `npm test`.
+
+## Discount codes
+
+An order takes one discount code at most, applied with `applyCode(orderNumber, code)`; a second code replaces the
+first. A refused code leaves the order as it was.
+
+- `SPRING10` takes 10 % off the order's items, rounded to the nearest cent (a half cent rounds up).
+- `WELCOME5` takes 5.00 € off the order's items, on an order whose items come to 30.00 € or more.
+
+The discount never touches shipping. Whether an order ships free is decided on its items before the discount, so a
+discount cannot lose an order its free shipping. An order's totals show the discount as `discountCents`, and
+`totalCents` is the items, less the discount, plus the shipping.
